   "what": "official SteamOS support for NVIDIA GPUs is being built; Valve team works with NVIDIA",
   "period": "Griffais does not expect anything before 2027",
   "status": "plan"
  },
  "draws": {
   "A1": [
    "Valve has confirmed that it has a growing team closely working with Team Green to bring official support for Nvidia GPUs. This comes from Valve engineer Pierre-Loup Griffais himself, who said in his interview with Verge that the company is working with AMD, Intel, and Nvidia to make the SteamOS experience better on a wider range of hardware. In his Bluesky post , he also said, \"If you have an AMD GPU, you can build your own Steam Machine now! More GPU support being worked on.\"",
    "over 90% of PC gamers using Team Green hardware still feel like second-class citizens on SteamOS."
   ],
