    "Valve engineer Pierre-Loup Griffais himself, who said in his interview with Verge that the company is working with AMD, Intel, and Nvidia to make the SteamOS experience better on a wider range of hardware. In his Bluesky post , he also said, \"If you have an AMD GPU, you can build your own Steam Machine now! More GPU support being worked on.\" With the SteamOS installation image updated to version 3.8.10 , Valve has expanded support to more AMD-powered handhelds and AMD discrete GPUs. The Nvidia rollout, however, will take time, as noted by Griffais. He doesn't expect anything before 2027, so Nvidia users have to wait, relying on Bazzite in the meantime."
