    "Readers may notice the huge gap between CoreWeave 5y unsecured bonds at ~10% and the 5.9% that CoreWeave paid for the fixed-rate tranche of their DDTL 4.0 $8.5B delayed-draw term loan, which was backstopped by Meta. This 5.9% yield works out to about 90 basis points wider than Meta’s 5y bond yield of ~5.0%."
